# The Dockerfile copies exactly four things: requirements.txt, app/, scripts/,
# and evals/events/. Everything else in this directory was being uploaded to
# the builder for no reason -- 265MB of context, of which 213MB was the local
# virtualenv and 44MB was eval corpora and snapshots.
#
# The one that matters beyond speed: backend/.env holds a real OPENAI_API_KEY,
# and while the Dockerfile never COPYs it, it was still being shipped to the
# remote builder on every deploy. It should never have left the machine.

# Local virtualenv -- the image installs its own from requirements.txt, and a
# macOS venv would not work in a linux container anyway.
venv/
.venv/

# Secrets. Never in a build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Test suite and its fixtures: the image runs the app, not the tests.
tests/

# Eval corpora, labels, snapshots and cached model responses. Only
# evals/events is copied (S4 reads it for offline report validation), so
# exclude the directory wholesale and re-include that one subtree.
evals/*
!evals/events/

# Build and tool artefacts.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Deployment configs are read by flyctl from outside the image.
fly.toml
fly.*.toml

# Logs and local scratch.
*.log
.DS_Store
